Previous coordination:
P1-W3 merged as PR #107. 262 tests pass on main at 1e50a92. No in-flight packets or open PRs. Selecting P1-W4 — the dual-write compatibility layer that bridges V1 wallet ingestion to V2 canonical storage. This is the critical compatibility packet: every write to V1 tables (transactions, indexer_checkpoints) must also populate V2 tables (raw_transactions, target_matches, checkpoints) with an auto-created wallet IndexTarget. The dual-write lives in the repository layer per RFC Section 5.2. V2 writes are best-effort during early transition. Dependencies P1-W2 (V2 tables) and P1-W3 (V2 repo methods) are both merged.

Previous active packet runtime:
- stage: fix_review_feedback
- implementation: Added dual-write compatibility layer: V1→V2 conversion functions (chain-to-network mapping, transaction/checkpoint conversion, target match construction), ensure_wallet_target idempotent shim, best-effort V2 writes in CLI and API ingestion paths, 32 new unit tests, and tracked handoff doc. All 294 tests pass with zero regressions. No V1 signatures changed.
- validation: P1-W4 passes all validation checks. cargo fmt, clippy, and all 294 tests (262 baseline + 32 new) are clean with zero regressions. No V1 signatures, API handlers, or CLI flags were modified. Chain-to-network mapping matches Rollout Plan §2.4 exactly. V2 RawTransaction correctly strips user_id/wallet_address. Checkpoint JSONB cursors match P0-W3 §5-6. All V2 write failures are caught and logged without affecting the V1 path. ensure_wallet_target uses an idempotent lookup-or-create pattern. The handoff artifact is present and in sync with the implementation.
- PR state: Created PR #108 for P1-W4. Pushed branch to origin and opened PR against main with full description covering dual-write layer (5 files, 947 insertions), validation results (294 tests, clean fmt/clippy), and handoff artifact. PR is open and ready for review.
- local review: The dual-write compatibility layer is well-structured with clean separation, thorough unit tests (32 new, 294 total passing), and correct best-effort V2 error handling. All CI checks pass. One blocking issue: the Hyperliquid checkpoint cursor uses 'last_timestamp_ms' (with ms conversion) instead of the required 'last_timestamp' key — the ms conversion is explicitly post-P1-W4 per the review spec. Five non-blocking issues noted including a missing ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING in the upstream P1-W3 index_target INSERT, match_reason traceability, missing DB integration tests, defensive coding suggestions, and streaming path coverage.
- remote review: 1 blocking issue: Hyperliquid checkpoint cursor key must be 'last_timestamp' (raw seconds) not 'last_timestamp_ms' (ts*1000) — the ms conversion is post-P1-W4. All other review focus areas pass: conversion correctness, best-effort V2 writes, chain-to-network mapping, V1 method preservation, target match creation, and minimal API/CLI wiring. CI fully green.
